WEBVTT

00:00:04.540 --> 00:00:05.630
Sorry.

00:00:05.630 --> 00:00:07.880
The machine at the chest is too tight.

00:00:07.880 --> 00:00:10.580
We couldn't get the size right on short notice.

00:00:10.580 --> 00:00:11.750
It's fine.

00:00:11.750 --> 00:00:15.960
We'll be monitoring your vitals
and other info from here.

00:00:15.960 --> 00:00:19.500
The same info will appear
on the display on your helmet.

00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:22.000
Okay. Understood.

00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:25.540
Momoki.

00:00:25.540 --> 00:00:29.540
What if she refuses to be
put back in the Mizuhanome?

00:00:33.170 --> 00:00:38.500
I... have to protect the lives
of my subordinates.

00:00:41.630 --> 00:00:43.460
Take command, Mr. Matsuoka.

00:00:43.460 --> 00:00:45.080
Got it.

00:00:45.080 --> 00:00:46.750
Go get it done.

00:00:46.750 --> 00:00:48.460
See you again soon.

00:02:43.100 --> 00:02:45.100
How cruel.

00:02:45.100 --> 00:02:52.020
This id well must come from a killer whose
first memory is also something cruel.

00:02:52.020 --> 00:02:54.400
Take this!

00:03:05.770 --> 00:03:08.230
At least come at me without shouting.

00:03:08.230 --> 00:03:10.520
It ruins the element of surprise.

00:03:12.730 --> 00:03:15.600
And look, you woke him up.

00:03:15.600 --> 00:03:16.900
Shut it!

00:03:16.900 --> 00:03:19.770
Don't lecture me, you piece of shit!

00:03:26.900 --> 00:03:28.190
Oh dear.

00:03:28.190 --> 00:03:31.810
That dirty mouth is unbefitting
a brilliant detective...

00:03:31.810 --> 00:03:35.520
You remembered yourself,
didn't you, Narihisago Akihito?

00:03:35.520 --> 00:03:42.150
Yeah. It wouldn't be revenge if I took you out
not knowing who I am, would it?

00:03:42.150 --> 00:03:44.650
Revenge, huh?

00:03:44.650 --> 00:03:46.270
How frightful.

00:03:46.270 --> 00:03:50.310
We're both brilliant detectives,
and we're both serial killers.

00:03:50.310 --> 00:03:52.020
Can't we all just get along?

00:03:52.020 --> 00:03:54.980
We're not the same, you fucking bastard.

00:03:54.980 --> 00:03:56.850
I'm astonished.

00:03:56.850 --> 00:04:00.520
Just what distinguishes you from me?

00:04:00.520 --> 00:04:03.310
A brilliant detective is someone who inquires.

00:04:03.310 --> 00:04:08.770
I'm making inquiries into justice,
in my own way.

00:04:08.770 --> 00:04:12.690
And it's just that you don't understand that.

00:04:12.690 --> 00:04:13.940
Right?

00:04:19.650 --> 00:04:20.980
All right!

00:04:23.020 --> 00:04:24.440
You did it, Hondomachi!

00:04:24.440 --> 00:04:26.690
Hijiriido, Mr. Sakaido.

00:04:26.690 --> 00:04:29.480
In the well, please address me as Hijiriido.

00:04:29.480 --> 00:04:32.060
Oh, come on. That doesn't matter.

00:04:32.060 --> 00:04:34.560
That's a weird thing to fuss about.

00:04:39.560 --> 00:04:42.190
I swear, what an awful thing to do.

00:04:43.400 --> 00:04:45.770
But you see now, don't you?

00:04:45.770 --> 00:04:47.940
You two are the same as me.

00:04:47.940 --> 00:04:51.190
You're driven to kill and you snare others.

00:04:51.190 --> 00:04:56.020
Also, what people call justice depends on
the criteria they use to judge.

00:04:56.020 --> 00:04:58.440
Even if my justice can't be found here,

00:04:58.440 --> 00:05:01.690
it can be found outside this place, Narihisago.

00:05:01.690 --> 00:05:05.520
Unfortunately, I can no longer
return to the outside world.

00:05:05.520 --> 00:05:07.100
For that very reason,

00:05:07.100 --> 00:05:11.190
the Mizuhanome will repair my data.

00:05:13.440 --> 00:05:15.230
And Ms. Hondomachi.

00:05:15.230 --> 00:05:16.230
Excuse me.

00:05:16.230 --> 00:05:20.350
Do you prefer I address you as Ms. Hijiriido?

00:05:20.350 --> 00:05:25.100
You mustn't forget that you're
dealing with a brilliant detective.

00:05:25.100 --> 00:05:31.690
You used Fukuda Tamotsu's abilities
to escape your well, did you not?

00:05:31.690 --> 00:05:34.190
It's thanks to him that I escaped.

00:05:34.190 --> 00:05:37.440
But that doesn't mean I used him.

00:05:40.270 --> 00:05:44.440
A gentleman's hat is of great importance.

00:05:46.440 --> 00:05:50.480
I suppose that was meant to provoke me.

00:05:50.480 --> 00:05:52.310
I guess I'll play along.

00:05:57.940 --> 00:05:59.850
Are you okay, Momoki?

00:05:59.850 --> 00:06:02.480
My head started to spin upon entering.

00:06:02.480 --> 00:06:04.190
Some slight nausea.

00:06:04.190 --> 00:06:09.980
It would appear that Asukai Kiki's powers
have grown, and the suit can't keep up.

00:06:09.980 --> 00:06:12.730
Even so, it's all we've got.

00:06:12.730 --> 00:06:14.100
I'll hurry.

00:06:25.480 --> 00:06:27.560
Oh yeah!

00:06:29.900 --> 00:06:31.520
Mr. Narihisago!

00:06:39.310 --> 00:06:43.060
Do they think playing hide and seek
will accomplish something?

00:06:52.230 --> 00:06:54.650
Hey, hey, hey, hey!

00:06:54.650 --> 00:06:56.650
You've gotta be kidding me!

00:07:17.850 --> 00:07:18.730
There it is!

00:07:18.730 --> 00:07:20.350
Past that house!

00:07:22.100 --> 00:07:23.810
Why you!

00:07:38.480 --> 00:07:43.560
Revenge is to be executed
more elegantly, Narihisago.

00:07:43.560 --> 00:07:45.270
Asshole.

00:07:45.270 --> 00:07:46.270
Mr. Narihisago.

00:07:46.270 --> 00:07:49.190
Please, don't strain yourself.

00:07:49.190 --> 00:07:51.480
You can stay seated.

00:07:51.480 --> 00:07:54.850
Let's calm down and take some time to talk.

00:07:54.850 --> 00:07:55.900
So?

00:07:55.900 --> 00:07:57.940
Where's Fukuda?

00:07:57.940 --> 00:08:01.520
You went to all the trouble of
luring me into <i>his</i> id well.

00:08:01.520 --> 00:08:05.270
He's on standby to cause a well storm, isn't he?

00:08:05.270 --> 00:08:06.100
Of course,

00:08:06.100 --> 00:08:12.440
I can't imagine he could serve as a third pillar
to take down a brilliant detective.

00:08:12.440 --> 00:08:16.650
Well, just you wait. It's gonna surprise you.

00:08:16.650 --> 00:08:19.900
What, another unsophisticated surprise attack?

00:08:19.900 --> 00:08:23.400
Hmm. I don't know about that.

00:08:28.060 --> 00:08:29.560
He still hasn't noticed.

00:08:29.560 --> 00:08:33.850
You mustn't forget he's
dealing with brilliant detectives.

00:08:35.980 --> 00:08:37.480
Hey now.

00:08:37.480 --> 00:08:38.690
What's wrong?

00:08:38.690 --> 00:08:42.100
I thought we were taking some time to talk.

00:08:44.770 --> 00:08:46.520
That's more like it.

00:08:46.520 --> 00:08:48.100
Mr. Narihisago.

00:08:48.100 --> 00:08:50.190
Let me do the honors.

00:08:51.770 --> 00:08:53.810
But first...

00:08:53.810 --> 00:08:58.020
Does the number seven
mean something to you, Mr. Uraido,

00:08:58.020 --> 00:09:01.810
or should I say Chief Hayaseura?

00:09:01.810 --> 00:09:03.810
Seven is a divine number.

00:09:03.810 --> 00:09:06.400
Even setting the Bible aside--

00:09:06.400 --> 00:09:08.230
I knew it.

00:09:08.230 --> 00:09:11.230
So it's a god complex type thing.

00:09:13.310 --> 00:09:21.020
I'll believe you meant it when you said
you have your own sense of justice.

00:09:21.020 --> 00:09:26.020
Chief Hayaseura, you limited not only
your serial killers' victims to seven,

00:09:26.020 --> 00:09:30.520
but your serial killers as well.

00:09:30.520 --> 00:09:35.730
You intended to cut it off at seven
and commit suicide.

00:09:35.730 --> 00:09:38.100
The Challenger, Thigh-severer, Face-lifter,

00:09:38.100 --> 00:09:41.480
Tongue-tearer, Gravedigger,
Arm-twister, and Perforator...

00:09:41.480 --> 00:09:45.020
But then I created an eighth serial killer.

00:09:45.020 --> 00:09:47.810
I created the Cornerer, did I not?

00:09:47.810 --> 00:09:51.020
I'm being called the "Cornerer"?

00:09:51.020 --> 00:09:54.060
Mr. Narihisago is not a serial killer.

00:09:54.060 --> 00:09:58.940
To be precise, he's a serial suicide inciter
who kills serial killers.

00:09:58.940 --> 00:10:03.980
In other words, to make sure
you would be cornered in the end...

00:10:03.980 --> 00:10:06.600
...you created a Cornerer.

00:10:06.600 --> 00:10:07.650
Ridiculous!

00:10:07.650 --> 00:10:13.100
His serial killer rule applies
directly to him, too.

00:10:13.100 --> 00:10:14.770
No more than seven victims.

00:10:14.770 --> 00:10:18.650
Once the limit is reached,
it's death or arrest. I see.

00:10:18.650 --> 00:10:20.690
You're wrong! I did no such thing!

00:10:20.690 --> 00:10:22.690
However badly you want to deny it,

00:10:22.690 --> 00:10:26.230
you can't deny the possibility
you acted unconsciously.

00:10:27.230 --> 00:10:31.560
As a brilliant detective,
I'll believe your sense of justice.

00:10:31.560 --> 00:10:35.730
And to foil your despicable plot,

00:10:35.730 --> 00:10:39.440
I won't let Mr. Narihisago
play the role you've given him.

00:10:39.440 --> 00:10:42.310
You manipulated everyone as if you were a god.

00:10:42.310 --> 00:10:46.600
But your plan won't
come to fruition on any level.

00:10:52.020 --> 00:10:53.440
What's happening?

00:10:53.440 --> 00:10:57.520
You're right. The surprise attack
does work better if I don't shout.

00:10:57.520 --> 00:10:59.310
I learned something.

00:10:59.310 --> 00:11:02.980
Mr. Uraido--no, Mr. Hayaseura.

00:11:02.980 --> 00:11:07.100
It's like they say: Management fails
because they don't know the work.

00:11:07.100 --> 00:11:10.020
Or maybe it's just easier for me to see,

00:11:10.020 --> 00:11:15.100
because the hole in my head affected
my perception of missing pieces.

00:11:15.100 --> 00:11:20.150
The thing you're sitting in is no chair.

00:11:20.150 --> 00:11:22.400
All I see...

00:11:22.400 --> 00:11:28.440
...is a Mizuhanome cockpit that brilliant
detective Anaido brought into this well.

00:11:30.100 --> 00:11:33.190
This is the support Fukuda Tamotsu provided,

00:11:33.190 --> 00:11:34.600
as the third pillar.

00:11:34.600 --> 00:11:37.230
Some elegantly executed revenge.

00:11:37.230 --> 00:11:38.230
Don't.

00:11:38.230 --> 00:11:41.190
Don't do this!

00:11:47.350 --> 00:11:52.650
At what point in that collapsing well
do you think Mr. Hayaseura will appear?

00:11:52.650 --> 00:11:55.810
You showed up just before
you went to Fukuda's house.

00:11:55.810 --> 00:11:56.980
And I...

00:11:56.980 --> 00:12:03.190
Yeah, I suppose he'll also arrive at
the point before his first kill.

00:12:07.600 --> 00:12:08.980
Help me!

00:12:08.980 --> 00:12:11.400
He's John Walker!

00:12:18.840 --> 00:12:20.220
What do we do?

00:12:20.400 --> 00:12:22.340
I'm not too sure.

00:12:22.340 --> 00:12:25.600
The detective in me is a little lost.

00:12:26.960 --> 00:12:29.300
Anyway we did it.

00:12:29.600 --> 00:12:32.600
You're right.

00:12:33.300 --> 00:12:34.300
Let's find out.

00:12:36.850 --> 00:12:41.600
Good. Now no one will accidentally
push the eject button.

00:12:41.600 --> 00:12:46.400
Thus did peace return to the world.

00:12:46.400 --> 00:12:48.600
Now we just have to get out.

00:12:48.600 --> 00:12:50.600
How?

00:12:50.600 --> 00:12:52.850
Do you have a plan?

00:12:52.850 --> 00:12:55.650
Nope. Just hope and anticipation.

00:12:55.650 --> 00:12:59.150
What?! We're brilliant detectives.

00:12:59.150 --> 00:13:04.150
Aren't we supposed to use our brains
to break out of any predicaments?

00:13:04.150 --> 00:13:09.440
The entirety of my knowledge is what
leads me to embrace hope and anticipation.

00:13:09.440 --> 00:13:16.650
Sometimes it's important to place your hopes
in a third party in another world.

00:13:16.650 --> 00:13:18.650
It's something that...

00:13:18.650 --> 00:13:21.060
...I've experienced as a brilliant detective.

00:13:33.650 --> 00:13:35.980
Brain function has dropped to 70%!

00:13:35.980 --> 00:13:37.400
His mind is fogged!

00:13:37.400 --> 00:13:39.400
150 cc's of the activator drug.

00:13:39.400 --> 00:13:41.270
His body can't handle that!

00:13:41.270 --> 00:13:42.310
Do it.

00:13:44.190 --> 00:13:45.150
Do it.

00:13:45.150 --> 00:13:46.980
If you won't, let me.

00:13:56.440 --> 00:13:59.270
Cardiac arrest! Vomit in the respiratory tract!

00:13:59.270 --> 00:14:00.730
Start chest compressions!

00:14:00.730 --> 00:14:03.100
Is the defibrillator ready?

00:14:06.150 --> 00:14:07.440
Still no pulse!

00:14:07.440 --> 00:14:08.900
Do it again!

00:14:10.020 --> 00:14:12.480
Defibrillate again!

00:14:12.480 --> 00:14:14.770
Administer adrenaline!

00:14:14.770 --> 00:14:16.770
Broken ribs are damaging the lungs!

00:14:16.770 --> 00:14:19.230
Ignore it! Keep going!

00:14:19.230 --> 00:14:21.560
Still no pulse! Comminuted rib fracture!

00:14:21.560 --> 00:14:22.650
Mr. Momoki!

00:14:22.650 --> 00:14:25.560
More adrenaline! Continue defibrillation!

00:14:33.270 --> 00:14:35.190
Pulse regained!

00:14:36.560 --> 00:14:37.900
Momoki!

00:14:38.770 --> 00:14:40.440
Momoki, you okay?

00:14:40.440 --> 00:14:42.770
Got all the vomit out?

00:14:42.770 --> 00:14:44.940
I'll manage.

00:14:44.940 --> 00:14:47.270
Also, Mr. Matsuoka.

00:14:47.270 --> 00:14:48.770
You're too loud.

00:14:48.770 --> 00:14:50.060
Sorry!

00:14:53.270 --> 00:14:56.020
But that's how I'm holding on.

00:15:20.150 --> 00:15:21.100
Mr. Matsuoka.

00:15:21.100 --> 00:15:23.850
Yeah. We see her, too.

00:15:24.980 --> 00:15:26.730
Keep up the drugs.

00:15:35.400 --> 00:15:37.400
It's you.

00:15:37.400 --> 00:15:38.980
Ms. Asukai.

00:15:39.940 --> 00:15:42.600
You're safe now.

00:15:42.600 --> 00:15:46.060
You came to save me again!

00:15:48.730 --> 00:15:50.350
Thank you so mu--

00:15:59.520 --> 00:16:01.270
Of course.

00:16:01.270 --> 00:16:04.600
I'm broken, aren't I?

00:16:04.600 --> 00:16:07.270
And putting those around me to sleep.

00:16:10.100 --> 00:16:13.150
I'm sure they're having horrific dreams.

00:16:14.480 --> 00:16:16.150
It's the same.

00:16:21.440 --> 00:16:23.190
As last time.

00:16:35.650 --> 00:16:37.980
I never stopped searching.

00:16:42.770 --> 00:16:45.560
For... me?

00:16:45.560 --> 00:16:46.940
Ms. Asukai.

00:16:49.350 --> 00:16:52.270
Do you... want to run away from here?

00:16:53.230 --> 00:16:54.850
Momoki! Hey!

00:16:57.350 --> 00:16:58.730
Dammit!

00:17:00.940 --> 00:17:03.440
And find someplace...

00:17:03.440 --> 00:17:06.270
...far away, with no other people around...

00:17:07.730 --> 00:17:12.310
...a place where you can't
reach others' dreams...

00:17:12.310 --> 00:17:16.690
...and live there? It might be an option.

00:17:18.440 --> 00:17:21.400
If there is such a place...

00:17:21.400 --> 00:17:25.150
...that might be a nice life.

00:17:25.150 --> 00:17:31.520
So, would you occasionally
visit me in that suit?

00:17:35.900 --> 00:17:40.690
It wouldn't work out, for either of us.

00:17:40.690 --> 00:17:42.440
Besides...

00:17:42.440 --> 00:17:48.350
I've recently started getting nightmares
from people in distant countries.

00:17:49.560 --> 00:17:52.270
My dream world has just...

00:17:52.270 --> 00:17:56.980
...steadily grown larger and larger, it seems.

00:18:03.900 --> 00:18:07.520
Shoot me with this.

00:18:07.520 --> 00:18:11.350
End all my suffering.

00:18:11.350 --> 00:18:15.900
It's what I asked of you when we first met.

00:18:35.060 --> 00:18:36.350
I can't.

00:18:37.400 --> 00:18:39.600
I'm a police officer.

00:18:43.150 --> 00:18:48.350
In the end... everyone keeps saying that.

00:18:48.350 --> 00:18:51.310
It's devastating to me.

00:18:52.350 --> 00:18:56.440
That you all want to save me,

00:18:56.440 --> 00:19:00.520
and no one will kill me
and put an end to my misery.

00:19:00.520 --> 00:19:01.600
I'm sorry.

00:19:01.600 --> 00:19:04.060
Please, don't apologize.

00:19:04.060 --> 00:19:06.150
It's not your fault.

00:19:08.060 --> 00:19:10.270
I know.

00:19:11.480 --> 00:19:14.020
I have to go back in, don't I?

00:19:15.100 --> 00:19:19.150
If I do, then at least...

00:19:19.150 --> 00:19:21.480
...I can be of use to someone.

00:19:27.270 --> 00:19:30.440
But for all my increased suffering,

00:19:30.440 --> 00:19:35.980
some part of me is more at peace than before.

00:19:37.560 --> 00:19:41.100
It's like I'll find
greater and greater relief...

00:19:41.100 --> 00:19:43.980
...floating in that darkness...

00:19:43.980 --> 00:19:50.770
...in deep, deep sleep--
so deep that I forget who I am.

00:19:53.310 --> 00:19:58.350
And anyway, there's nothing for me,

00:19:58.350 --> 00:20:01.600
not here,

00:20:01.600 --> 00:20:03.270
not anywhere.

00:20:05.940 --> 00:20:07.400
Ms. Asukai.

00:20:13.310 --> 00:20:15.100
Ms. Asukai.

00:20:15.100 --> 00:20:19.310
We... can't free you yet.

00:20:20.730 --> 00:20:23.520
But someday...

00:20:23.520 --> 00:20:25.480
I swear...

00:20:25.480 --> 00:20:27.770
One day...

00:20:27.770 --> 00:20:32.100
Someone will come along who can truly save you!

00:20:33.690 --> 00:20:37.150
Please, wait for that day.

00:20:38.400 --> 00:20:40.810
Don't give up hope.

00:20:40.810 --> 00:20:42.150
Someday...

00:20:42.150 --> 00:20:46.020
You'll be released from your suffering!

00:20:46.020 --> 00:20:47.980
I'll make sure of it!

00:20:50.900 --> 00:20:52.980
Hey.

00:20:52.980 --> 00:20:56.350
This is the first time I've found you alive.

00:20:58.060 --> 00:20:59.690
Kaeru.

00:21:05.060 --> 00:21:08.600
I... believe you.

00:21:09.850 --> 00:21:13.150
So I'll be waiting, right here.

00:21:15.440 --> 00:21:16.940
As long as it takes.

00:21:39.060 --> 00:21:40.600
Where are we?

00:21:42.980 --> 00:21:44.480
We're saved!

00:21:44.480 --> 00:21:47.020
Yeah. Looks like it.

00:21:49.060 --> 00:21:51.150
Is it safe to talk now?

00:21:52.060 --> 00:21:56.270
Sakaido and Hijiriido are alive in the well!

00:21:56.270 --> 00:21:57.770
Extract them!

00:22:04.440 --> 00:22:05.480
Don't panic!

00:22:05.480 --> 00:22:07.480
Call the medical unit.

00:22:09.600 --> 00:22:11.190
Hondomachi.

00:22:15.770 --> 00:22:16.850
It's all right.

00:22:16.850 --> 00:22:20.440
Cry while you can.

00:22:20.440 --> 00:22:25.980
No. I think one tear is just right for him.

00:22:28.900 --> 00:22:30.650
All right then.

00:22:30.650 --> 00:22:33.980
You're coming back home, right?

00:22:34.980 --> 00:22:36.400
Yeah.

00:22:37.770 --> 00:22:39.650
One day, for sure.

00:22:39.650 --> 00:22:42.480
I'll go back to my real one.

00:22:42.480 --> 00:22:45.940
It's just not going to be now.

00:22:49.520 --> 00:22:52.230
It's also a joy to run out of tears.

00:22:54.600 --> 00:22:58.900
And so the curtain closed
on the John Walker case.

00:23:00.900 --> 00:23:06.440
Hayaseura Takuhiko's death was handled
as a suicide caused by mental breakdown.

00:23:06.440 --> 00:23:10.150
The truth of the Mizuhanome
was once again concealed.

00:23:12.020 --> 00:23:15.730
The true nature of the case, the victims,

00:23:15.730 --> 00:23:20.940
and the existence of comatose personnel
who have yet to wake up--

00:23:20.940 --> 00:23:23.690
none of it would be made public.

00:23:24.940 --> 00:23:30.480
All personnel knew that was the way
the Kura organization worked.

00:23:30.480 --> 00:23:37.190
Whatever happens here--be it a past event
or a workplace secret--is stored away.

00:23:39.600 --> 00:23:43.190
Narihisago and Hondomachi, are you ready?

00:23:43.190 --> 00:23:44.730
All set!

00:23:46.020 --> 00:23:48.060
Are you up to this, Narihisago?

00:23:48.060 --> 00:23:49.810
Yes, no problem.

00:23:49.810 --> 00:23:51.560
This one is a new id well.

00:23:51.560 --> 00:23:52.980
Keep your wits about you.

00:23:52.980 --> 00:23:53.850
Of course.

00:23:53.850 --> 00:23:56.900
But when we dive, we won't be ourselves.

00:23:56.900 --> 00:23:58.940
I wonder, will that make a difference?

00:23:58.940 --> 00:24:01.850
You're gonna make it make a difference, Koharu.

00:24:01.850 --> 00:24:04.020
Roger! I'll do my best!

00:24:04.020 --> 00:24:07.230
I'm excited to see a new killer's id well.

00:24:07.230 --> 00:24:09.900
Good luck with <i>your</i> end of the case, everyone!

00:24:09.900 --> 00:24:12.480
She sure is an oddball.

00:24:13.520 --> 00:24:16.850
Looks like she's the right person
in the right place.

00:24:16.850 --> 00:24:18.440
Come on, rookie!

00:24:19.690 --> 00:24:21.020
Sorry I'm late.

00:24:21.020 --> 00:24:22.850
We have our authorization.

00:24:22.850 --> 00:24:24.020
Understood.

00:24:24.020 --> 00:24:26.980
The new system will have kinks for some time.

00:24:26.980 --> 00:24:29.730
But you'll handle it, Acting Chief.

00:24:29.730 --> 00:24:30.940
Yes, sir!

00:24:30.940 --> 00:24:34.060
Didn't he say we'd be working in shifts?

00:24:34.060 --> 00:24:35.900
This time you'll be partnered.

00:24:35.900 --> 00:24:40.310
The real-world investigation
takes priority over the id well mystery.

00:24:40.310 --> 00:24:43.100
This ups the quality and amount of information,

00:24:43.100 --> 00:24:44.560
and analysis efficiency.

00:24:44.560 --> 00:24:46.940
Got it.

00:24:46.940 --> 00:24:49.270
All right. Inject them!

00:24:51.230 --> 00:24:55.600
Their voices don't reach me.

00:24:55.600 --> 00:25:00.600
Even if I could hear them,
I wouldn't know who spoke.

00:25:00.600 --> 00:25:06.940
I stop being myself, and my new self
doesn't even know who I am.

00:25:06.940 --> 00:25:11.940
And when I open my eyes
as if I'm about to die again,

00:25:11.940 --> 00:25:15.270
I always find myself in a strange world.

00:25:15.270 --> 00:25:19.350
The same girl is always there,
but she's already dead.

00:25:19.350 --> 00:25:22.520
She's been killed. There's a mystery.

00:25:22.520 --> 00:25:29.400
And then, that girl tells me my name and my job.

00:25:29.400 --> 00:25:32.310
That's how I come to understand.

00:25:32.310 --> 00:25:35.770
That everything in this world means something.

00:25:35.770 --> 00:25:38.150
That my life means something,

00:25:38.150 --> 00:25:40.770
and that her death means something, too.

00:25:40.770 --> 00:25:44.020
There's a job that can
only be done in that world,

00:25:44.020 --> 00:25:47.900
and I'm the only one who can finish it.

00:25:47.900 --> 00:25:50.560
My name is Sakaido.

00:25:55.900 --> 00:25:57.690
I'm a brilliant detective.
